---
// Terms of Use (2026-11-05). Plain language, general U.S. contract terms, no statute claims. Every value
// only the owner can decide comes from site.legal in src/config/site.ts; until all are set, LegalStatus
// shows the review banner.
import Breadcrumbs from "@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import LegalStatus from "@/components/LegalStatus.astro";
import LegalValue from "@/components/LegalValue.astro";
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site, sitePath } from "@/config/site";

const { legal } = site;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use | 559 Solutions"
  description="The Terms of Use for the 559 Solutions website, its articles, worksheets, Code559 lessons and digital products."
  canonicalPath="/terms/"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Terms of Use" }]} />
      <p class="eyebrow">Site information</p>
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="lede">The rules for using this website and what it offers.</p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="section">
    <article class="narrow legal-content">
      <LegalStatus />

      <h2>Agreement</h2>
      <p>
        These terms apply when you use 559solutions.com. By using the site, you accept them. If you do not agree, please do
        not use the site.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        This site is run by <LegalValue value={legal.legalName} />, doing business as 559 Solutions. In these terms, "we" and
        "us" mean 559 Solutions. You can reach us through the <a href={sitePath("/contact/")}>contact form</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Using the site</h2>
      <p>Use the site only for lawful purposes. Please do not:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>scrape or copy the site in a way that slows it down or harms it;</li>
        <li>try to get around its security or reach parts of it you are not meant to;</li>
        <li>misuse the forms, for example by sending spam, false information or someone else's details.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Content and ownership</h2>
      <p>
        The site's text, articles, lessons, diagrams and design belong to us, unless a page says otherwise. You may read,
        print and use them for your own learning and inside your own business. To republish them, on another site or in
        anything you sell or share publicly, ask us first.
      </p>
      <p>Some Code559 lessons include material from others under these licenses, as each lesson notes:</p>
      <blockquote class="legal-quote">
        <p>
          <em>
            Code559 is a 559 Solutions project. Portions adapted from Visual Studio Code documentation (CC BY 3.0 US),
            GitHub Docs (CC BY 4.0), and GitHub Skills (MIT). Screenshots used with permission from Microsoft.
          </em>
        </p>
      </blockquote>
      <p>Those portions stay under their own licenses. Some Code559 icons come from Lucide, under the MIT license.</p>

      <h2>Worksheets and tools</h2>
      <p>
        The worksheets, self-checks and other tools on this site run in your browser. What you type and the results you get
        are yours. They are aids for thinking, not answers. We do not promise that a result fits any decision you make.
      </p>

      <h2>Digital products</h2>
      <p>
        Digital products, such as the Code559 module packets, are sold through Gumroad. Gumroad's own terms also apply when
        you check out there.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each product's license is stated on its page. The licenses published on this site so far let the buyer use the
        product inside their own organization, and do not allow resale or redistribution of the blank files.
      </p>
      <p>After you buy, Gumroad gives you a download link for the files.</p>
      <p><strong>Refunds:</strong> <LegalValue value={legal.refundPolicy} /></p>

      <h2>Services</h2>
      <p>
        The services described on this site are for information only. Nothing on the site is an offer to provide a service.
        Each engagement is covered by its own written agreement. If that agreement and these terms disagree, the agreement
        controls.
      </p>

      <h2>Not professional advice</h2>
      <p>
        Articles, guides and lessons are general education. They are not legal, financial, security or other professional
        advice. For advice about your own situation, talk to a qualified professional. Information about tools is current as
        of the date shown with it, and tools change.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>
        The site links to sites run by others. We do not control those sites, and a link does not mean we endorse them or
        what they offer.
      </p>

      <h2>What you send us</h2>
      <p>
        When you send us something through a form, you confirm that you have the right to send it. Please do not send
        confidential or sensitive information, such as passwords, payment details, health information or private client
        data, through the forms.
      </p>

      <h2>Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
      <p>
        The site and everything on it are provided "as is" and "as available." We do not promise that the site will always
        be available or free of errors, or that its content is complete or right for your purpose.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect, incidental, special or consequential damages, such as
        lost profits or lost data, that come from your use of the site or its content. To the extent the law allows, our
        total liability for any claim is limited to the greater of the amount you paid for the product the claim is about,
        or $100.
      </p>

      <h2>Indemnity</h2>
      <p>
        If someone makes a claim against us because you misused the site or broke these terms, you agree to cover our
        reasonable costs from that claim. This applies only to claims caused by your misuse or breach.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes and ending access</h2>
      <p>
        We may change these terms. When we do, we will post the new version here with a new effective date. Using the site
        after that means you accept the new terms. We may suspend or end access for anyone who misuses the site.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law and venue</h2>
      <p>
        The laws of the State of <LegalValue value={legal.governingLawState} /> govern these terms. Any legal case about
        these terms will be brought in the courts located in <LegalValue value={legal.venueCounty} />,{" "}
        <LegalValue value={legal.governingLawState} />.
      </p>

      <h2>General</h2>
      <p>
        If a court finds part of these terms unenforceable, the rest still applies. If we do not enforce a term right away,
        we have not given up the right to enforce it later. These terms, together with each product's page and any signed
        service agreement, are the whole agreement between you and us about the site.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms? Use the <a href={sitePath("/contact/")}>contact form</a>, or write to{" "}
        <LegalValue value={legal.legalName} />, <LegalValue value={legal.businessAddress} />.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
